Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coff64-rs6000.c
Line: 792
Function: xcoff64_reloc_type_br
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: Uses rel->r_symndx to index obj_xcoff_sym_hashes(input_bfd) without validating the upper bound. Only a lower-bound check (rel->r_symndx >= 0) is performed (line 789). A crafted relocation with an out-of-range symbol index can cause an out-of-bounds read of the hash array, leading to an invalid pointer h and subsequent dereferences.

